DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppnnggttooppnnmm  was  obsoleted  by  ppnnggttooppaamm(1), introduced with Netpbm 10.44
       (September 2008).  ppnnggttooppaamm is backward compatible with ppnnggttooppnnmm,  plus
       adds  many additional functions, including the ability to produce a PAM
       image that includes a transparency (alpha) channel.

       Starting in Release 10.48, ppnnggttooppnnmm is just an alias for ppnnggttooppaamm.

       ppnnggttooppnnmm remained in the Netpbm package through Release  10.47  because
       it  may  have  fewer  bugs  than ppnnggttooppaamm in those releases, and may be
       faster in some environments.  But ppnnggttooppnnmm's incompatibility  with  the
       most  current PNG libraries makes it impractical to maintain along with
       ppnnggttooppaamm now.

       In releases before 10.48, you can use the  ppnnggttooppaamm  documentation  for
       ppnnggttooppnnmm, considering the following differences:




       •      ppnnggttooppnnmm  options  are  a  subset  of  ppnnggttooppaamm's, as documented
              above.


       •      Any change that the ppnnggttooppaamm manual says happened  in  or  after
              Netpbm 10.44 doesn't apply to ppnnggttooppnnmm.

